# MCP Integration Lab conventions

Read `AGENTS.md` for the full rules. Non-negotiables:

- Team-variable config (ports, mode, storage, service YAML/JSON) lives in
  `profiles/<name>/`, never hardcoded in compose files. `.env` selects the
  profile; process env > `.env` > `profile.env`.
- Runtime state is ephemeral: `make reset` must wipe it; the profile is the
  source of truth (`make register` reapplies gateway config).
- Orchestration lives in the Go CLI (`cmd/mcplab` + `internal/`). No new bash
  lifecycle scripts.
- Service ports publish on all interfaces (remote systems test against this
  lab); host ports are profile-defined and auth stays on (bearer/TLS).
- Never commit `secrets/` or edit `third_party/` directly — vendored changes go in
  `patches/` (applied by `mcplab vendor`) and get PR'd upstream.
- Every service must be listed in the profile's `labinfo/services.yaml` with
 its web/REST URLs *and* a `connection` block (protocol endpoints, client
 parameters like DNs/zones/mount options, on-the-wire credentials) — the
 labinfo MCP tools `endpoints_list`/`connections_list` are how agents hand
 users URLs and configure clients, and labinfo refuses to start without the
 connection block. Credentials in that catalog are revealed only when the
 profile sets `LAB_DEV_MODE=true`, which also opens the gateway — never
 default a shared profile to dev mode.
- The mail sink never sends mail: leftover `maildev/maildev.yaml` and
  relay/outbound keys in `labmail/bootstrap.yaml` are rejected by
  `internal/maildev` — keep that guard fail-closed and tested.
- Docs ship with the change: README, architecture doc, AGENTS.md, CLI usage
  text, and the labinfo catalog must be updated in the same change that
  alters behavior — sweep for stale mentions before finishing.
- Every user-visible change lands with a high-level `CHANGELOG.md` entry
  under `[Unreleased]`; releases promote that section, so each release
  summarizes all changes since the last one.
- CI/test failures are investigated to root cause and hardened (regression
  test, fail-closed guard, or wait condition) — never just rerun until green.
- Acceptance gate: `make test` and `make up && make smoke` all green.
